CORE
a.c
b.c --forward-impact
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
\*\* compute \*\*
^-.*function compute
^\+.*function compute
^D.*function compute
--
^warning: ignoring
//
// --forward-impact propagates impact forward from the change. The D
// (data-dependence) line is what distinguishes it from --backward-impact (see
// backward-impact1), so assert it in addition to the syntactic-diff (-/+)
// markers.
